#: ../../running/console.rst:2 7b014e7368734b0485ceddd2f975bb38
msgid "The system console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:4 03fb05cac8e944f4a50ac25267c5b605
msgid ""
"Six pages about the host rather than about the libraries: what is "
"running, what the kernel sees, what is in the logs, and whether the disk "
"is filling up. This is where to look when a library misbehaves and the "
"library pages look fine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:9 9da683906f6a46a2b632c8b9cbe124fe
msgid "The system console, showing host facts, MHVTL services and modules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:18 c4a749c535e743c1bd16e05029e5b448
msgid "Console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:20 d6fd9a3e7118415bb35ee9f84ae7944b
msgid ""
"``/libraries/console/`` - the summary: the host, the MHVTL services, the "
"kernel modules, and how many SCSI devices there are."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:39 0330152618a7400e8a5269b1aa496fd3
msgid "Services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:41 d555351038ef404981a9c80369f8da5e
msgid "Every MHVTL unit: the target, one daemon per library, one per drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:55 fdb9ddbc2ff6471f8c969b126a80e389
msgid ""
"``healthy no`` with a count short of the total means a daemon is down. "
"The page names which, and so does ``systemctl``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:58 a4addd1025da441f8aa5edb1f760ea08
msgid "The services page: the target, the libraries and the drives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:68 21d1cd53056b47f580e2be315eabe420
msgid "Devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:70 b19ff7ea8f604b0f9ac3dcc4a357d7f5
msgid ""
"What the kernel sees, which is the ground truth underneath everything "
"MHVTL claims."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:83 2a2dca17096b4489bdb777aa2f6c9b80
msgid ""
"``mediumx`` is a robot, ``tape`` a drive. A changer has no ``/dev/st``, "
"so its generic node is the one everything uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:86 fd8fcc90926d425e933d74052eabbba6
msgid "The devices page: what the kernel sees"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:90 a823af6a932240488f53ad1d6512f0de
msgid "To go the other way - from a library or drive id to its device:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:105 c3af8ab0c4904d7c957dd413557dfdf3
msgid ""
"These numbers are not stable. They change when the MHVTL module reloads "
"and when a library is recreated, which is why anything that remembers a "
"device - an iSCSI export, for instance - has to be repointed afterwards. "
"See :doc:`../using/iscsi`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:111 af153c2a278240ff9822a3e5dc6fdea2
msgid "Modules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:128 101f9dfdf6b849c79c416ca16b9cb2b1
msgid ""
"Only ``mhvtl`` is required. The rest matter when exporting over iSCSI: "
"LIO loads what it needs, and a module that is missing shows up there as "
"an export that cannot be made."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:132 79c05762e220494c804ce607dfb2d72b
msgid ""
"The ``ch`` module is deliberately **not** in this list, and is "
"blacklisted on this host. It takes a reference on every drive a changer "
"reports and never gives it back, which makes those drives' SCSI addresses"
" unusable until the machine reboots. The guide *The kernel ch driver "
"leak* explains it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:138 e81ca283b54f44d591348365f7354e43
msgid "Logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:140 22b139016c5a42a0b255ac231e08286f
msgid ""
"An allowlisted set of logs, tailed - the console never reads an arbitrary"
" path off the disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:151 3303a62279344272b833e8cd0004b180
msgid ""
"MHVTL logs every SCSI command it is given, so this is verbose and useful "
"in equal measure: when a backup fails, the last few lines say what the "
"drive was asked to do and what it answered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:156 601c10d4548c4f0f8e18ad5900180b30
msgid "Disk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:158 05845e75d03343ed8b073b97146d44cb
msgid ""
"Tapes are files. When the disk fills, writes fail in ways that look like "
"drive faults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/console.rst:171 fa6b7739de6b481c9fba3c93a50e170a
msgid ""
"``/opt/mhvtl`` holds the cartridges, ``/etc/mhvtl`` the configuration. A "
"cartridge only occupies what has been written to it, not the size it was "
"created with - so a library of ten 500 GB tapes does not need five "
"terabytes until somebody writes that much."
msgstr ""

